# async function load(id: number) { await id; .. }   async function run(x: any) { return await load(x) }
# The tests at the head of a typed async function are a function of their own (role EntryChecks), which calls the ramp of the typed version in one arm and the ramp of the generic version in the other.
# A caller that has not proven its argument calls the tests. Where it awaits the result at once it takes the tests in, whatever the three functions weigh together: the two ramps then stand in the caller,
# InlineCalls leaves them alone, and ResolveAwaitedCalls enters either callee without a promise, as it does for the same function without types.
# A caller that does anything else with the promise decides as it does about any function behind tests
